CRUG - licensing status
========================

This repository is being built in two layers with different licensing
obligations. Read this before adding code.

1. Specification documents (spec/, docs/)
   Currently distributed under the MIT licence in LICENSE, Copyright (c) 2026
   CLEG0078. They contain no GCC source.

2. Compiler implementation (gcc/crug/ and any file derived from GCC)
   If this repository adopts the GCC fork plan, every file that is derived from
   or linked with GCC code must be GPLv3-or-later. That includes copyright
   headers such as:

       Copyright (C) 2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
       This file is part of GCC. GCC is free software; you can redistribute it
       and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as
       published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 3, or (at your
       option) any later version.

   Adding such code under MIT alone is a licence violation. This is recorded as
   conflict C-07 in spec/000-PRECEDENCE.md and is DECISION-REQUIRED by the
   project owner before the first line of GCC-derived code lands.

3. Runtime library (libcrug/)
   The licence is not yet selected. It must be chosen before libcrug ships,
   because it determines whether Crug-produced binaries can be linked into
   GPL-incompatible programs.

4. Generated and third-party content
   - Kernel corpus used for K0 qualification: GPLv2, must never be vendored into
     this repository; the corpus is a checked-out external tree referenced by
     pin file.
   - Benchmark inputs: licence must be recorded per benchmark in bench/NOTICE.

This NOTICE does not change LICENSE. It states the obligation that a GCC fork
creates.
